File Formats
Format	Extension	Encryption	Opened By	Use Case
Plain text	.txt	None	Any text editor	Sharing, interoperability
Encrypted	.stxt	AES-128 + PBKDF2 (100k)	Secure Text Editor only	Private notes, sensitive data
.stxt File Structure
text
STXT-ENC-V1:<base64-salt>:<fernet-token>
•	Header STXT-ENC-V1: – Identifies the format for auto-detection.
•	Salt – 16 random bytes, base64-encoded, unique per save.
•	Token – Fernet-encrypted ciphertext (AES-128-CBC + HMAC-SHA256).
Overhead
•	File size increases by ~33% due to base64 encoding.
•	A 50 MB document becomes ~66 MB on disk.
•	Memory peak during encrypt/decrypt: ~3× content size (50 MB → 150 MB).
