Who Is It For?
1. Privacy-Conscious Individuals
Keep personal journals, passwords, and private notes fully offline and encrypted on disk. Even if someone copies the file or steals your USB drive, they cannot read the contents without the master password. The lock overlay protects against shoulder-surfing when stepping away.
Why it fits: File-level encryption, one-key lock, fully offline.
2. Legal, Medical, and Financial Professionals
Handle confidential client information in a compliant manner. .stxt files provide encryption at rest, an audit trail records all actions, and read-only modes protect against accidental modification. Meets common confidentiality obligations (HIPAA, GDPR, attorney-client privilege).
Why it fits: Encryption at rest, audit trail, machine-bound licensing.
3. Writers, Authors, and Content Creators
Protect unpublished manuscripts from leaks. Encrypted storage ensures that a stolen laptop or synced folder cannot expose your drafts. Version history and automatic backups guard against accidental deletions.
Why it fits: Manuscript protection, version history, offline.
4. Programmers and Developers
A fast, lightweight alternative to bloated IDEs for code snippets, API keys, and credentials you'd rather not paste into a browser. Save as .stxt for secrets; .txt for everything else.
Why it fits: Encrypted storage for secrets, global shortcuts, offline.
5. Students and Researchers
Store thesis drafts, research data, and study notes securely on your own computer. Backups guard against loss; the audit log tracks changes.
Why it fits: Encryption, backup system, affordable one-time purchase.
6. Small Businesses and Teams
Equip staff with a secure offline editor for internal documents. Batch licensing and machine binding prevent sharing. Custom data directory supports shared network drives. Audit logs provide usage visibility.
Why it fits: Batch licensing, audit trail, network-friendly.
