Frequently Asked Questions
Q: What happens if I lose my master password?
A: Encrypted files cannot be decrypted. Plain .txt files remain accessible. Always back up the master password in a secure location.
Q: Can someone read my .stxt file if they know the path?
A: No. The file contains only an encrypted blob; without the master password, the content is unreadable.
Q: Can I open .stxt files in other editors?
A: No — only Secure Text Editor can decrypt them. This is by design.
Q: Does auto-backup leak plaintext?
A: Encrypted (.stxt) files are not backed up as plaintext. Only plain .txt files get plaintext backups.
Q: Can I use the same license on two computers?
A: No. Each license is bound to a machine code.
Q: What if I switch computers?
A: Contact the author with the new machine code to receive a new license.
Q: Does the editor sync to the cloud?
A: No. It never connects to the internet.
Q: Can I still use plain .txt files?
A: Yes — choose No at the save prompt, or use Save As Plain.
